<title>TURKEY: Turkish 1996 C/A deficit at 2.4 pct of GNP.</title>
<headline>Turkish 1996 C/A deficit at 2.4 pct of GNP.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's current account deficit of $4.39 billion made up 2.4 percent of the GNP last year, compared to a $2.34 billion deficit and a 1.4 percent share in 1995, the central bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Turkey's current account had produced a $2.63 billion surplus in 1994.</p>
<p>The release of current account data for 1996 was delayed due to technical problems in the calculation of foreign trade data caused by Turkey's customs Union with the European Union.</p>
<p>The central bank gave the following following figures for December 1996 and the whole year:</p>
<p>    ($ million)	   Dec96   Nov96   Dec95  Jan-Dec96 Jan-Dec95</p>
<p>Current account    -1,040    -788  -1,453    -4,393    -2,339</p>
<p>Exports fob	   2,430   2,184   2,418    23,461    21,975</p>
<p>Imports fob	  -4,375  -3,785  -4,189   -41,935   -35,187</p>
<p>  Gold imports	  -71    -124    -111    -1,672    -1,322</p>
<p>Foreign trade blnc -1,945  -1,601  -1,771   -18,474   -13,212</p>
<p>Invisible credit    1,730   1,463   1,152    20,527    16,094</p>
<p>  Tourism		 238     329     174     5,650     4,957</p>
<p>Invisible debit    -1,166    -971  -1,035   -10,893    -9,717</p>
